          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Penetrating densifiers are permanent — they become part of the concrete and don't need reapplication. Epoxy coatings typically hold up 5-10+ years under normal residential foot traffic before showing enough wear to warrant a fresh topcoat, though heavy equipment, rolling tool chests, or vehicle traffic will shorten that. Vapor barrier primer systems generally last as long as the topcoat applied over them, since the primer itself isn't exposed to wear.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "My basement floods occasionally — should I still seal the floor?",
