            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Not yet. Sealing over a slab that periodically takes on standing water is a waste of money — the water will find its way in around the coating's edges or through the source that caused the flooding in the first place, and epoxy coatings can actually trap moisture underneath and delaminate faster once flooding resumes. Solve the water intrusion first with drainage, grading, or a sump system (see our wet basement solutions guide), confirm the floor stays dry through at least one full rainy season, then seal.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      author: { "@type": "Person", name: "Alex Rivers" },
